{"jsonrpc": "2.0", "id": 35, "result": {"description": "Prove (or refute with a counterexample) that two expressions are equal", "messages": [{"role": "user", "content": {"type": "text", "text": "Decide whether x=x holds, with the ucas tools.  For polynomial or rational expressions use algebra simplify on the difference (an exact normal form is a proof; note any conditions where a factor cancelled).  For machine-typed expressions use analyze equiv (exhaustive over the domain, or a counterexample).  For trigonometric ones use complex trig, which checks each form.  State which kind of proof you got (symbolic, exhaustive, numeric)."}}]}}
